    <h1>morning-briefing — Skill Description Optimization</h1>
    <div class="explainer">
        <strong>Optimizing your skill's description.</strong> This page updates automatically as Claude tests different versions of your skill's description. Each row is an iteration — a new description attempt. The columns show test queries: green checkmarks mean the skill triggered correctly (or correctly didn't trigger), red crosses mean it got it wrong. The "Train" score shows performance on queries used to improve the description; the "Test" score shows performance on held-out queries the optimizer hasn't seen. When it's done, Claude will apply the best-performing description to your skill.
    </div>

    <div class="summary">
        <p><strong>Original:</strong> Daily intelligence briefing. Queries the work-intel knowledge base (ChromaDB) for today&#x27;s priorities across Jira, GitLab, Gmail, WhatsApp, Telegram, Google Drive, and Truewatch, then syncs any new delta items in the background. Produces a structured daily plan with 🔴 Must Do / 🟡 Should Do / 🔵 This Week / 🔔 Reminders sections. Use this skill whenever the user says &quot;good morning&quot;, &quot;what should I work on&quot;, &quot;daily briefing&quot;, &quot;morning briefing&quot;, &quot;what&#x27;s happening today&quot;, &quot;what&#x27;s my plan for today&quot;, &quot;give me a briefing&quot;, &quot;what&#x27;s going on&quot;, or any variation asking for situational awareness at the start of a workday.</p>
        <p class="best"><strong>Best:</strong> Daily intelligence briefing. Queries the work-intel knowledge base (ChromaDB) for today&#x27;s priorities across Jira, GitLab, Gmail, WhatsApp, Telegram, Google Drive, and Truewatch, then syncs any new delta items in the background. Produces a structured daily plan with 🔴 Must Do / 🟡 Should Do / 🔵 This Week / 🔔 Reminders sections. Use this skill whenever the user says &quot;good morning&quot;, &quot;what should I work on&quot;, &quot;daily briefing&quot;, &quot;morning briefing&quot;, &quot;what&#x27;s happening today&quot;, &quot;what&#x27;s my plan for today&quot;, &quot;give me a briefing&quot;, &quot;what&#x27;s going on&quot;, or any variation asking for situational awareness at the start of a workday.</p>
